Falsifies `device_tree_blob::verification::a_token_step_is_total_and_moves_forward`.

The defect: the token walk subtracts one from the depth at `FDT_END_NODE` with a bare
`depth - 1` in place of `checked_sub` and its `BadStructure` refusal. Every balanced tree walks the
same under both; a structure block that opens with `FDT_END_NODE`, which no compiler writes and any
hostile blob can, underflows the depth and panics the boot.

Expected to fail: the subtraction overflow check on `depth - 1`, for any accepted blob whose
structure block starts with token 2.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -1082,7 +1082,7 @@
                 }
                 FDT_END_NODE => {
                     let depth = self.depth;
-                    self.depth = depth.checked_sub(1).ok_or(Error::BadStructure)?;
+                    self.depth = depth - 1;
                     return Ok(Some((depth, Token::EndNode)));
                 }
                 FDT_PROP => {
